# repos.conf — repositories monitored by claude-worklog
#
# The worklog repo itself (this repo) is always included automatically.
# Add one line per additional repository your team uses.
#
# Format:  alias=absolute_path
#
# - alias: short name shown in session logs and day reports (no spaces)
# - path:  absolute path to the repository root (must contain a .git folder)
#
# Examples (Windows):
#   backend=C:\Users\yourname\Projects\my-backend
#   frontend=C:\Users\yourname\Projects\my-frontend
#   infra=C:\Users\yourname\Projects\my-infra
#
# Paths with spaces work without quoting:
#   data-pipeline=C:\Users\Jane Doe\Projects\My Data Pipeline
#
# Examples (WSL/Linux):
#   backend=/home/yourname/projects/my-backend
#   frontend=/home/yourname/projects/my-frontend
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-repository preference:  alias.worktree=yes|no
#
# Does this repository use a git worktree per demand, or does the work happen in the main copy on a
# branch named after the demand?
#
#   yes  work goes in a worktree under worklogs/<TICKET>/<alias>/
#   no   work goes in the main copy, on a branch named after the demand
#
# A fresh worktree is an empty working directory: everything git does not track has to be rebuilt
# there -- dependencies (node_modules, virtualenv), local .env files, generated clients, seeded local
# databases. For a small repository that costs seconds; for an application repository it is a full
# reinstall and reconfiguration on every demand, which is rework. That is why the answer belongs to
# each repository, and often to each machine.
#
# Leave the line out and Claude asks once, the first time it needs to change that repository for a
# demand, then records the answer here so it never asks again. To set or read it by hand:
#   .\scripts\repo-worktree.ps1 -Alias backend -Use no
#   .\scripts\repo-worktree.ps1                       # list all
#
#   backend=C:\Users\yourname\Projects\my-backend
#   backend.worktree=no
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Add your repositories below:
